    dc:type "resolution-route/computation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Define directness by a fixed algorithmic model and compare the time needed to generate trajectories under evolution rules with the time needed to find satisfying configurations for matched constraint families. Complexity lower bounds or efficient constructive algorithms would test restricted formal versions.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Constraint satisfaction ranges from trivial to undecidable.", "No single complexity statement covers all constraint systems.", "“Going outside the system” is metaphorical.";
